# why:      the first run (phase-524-w1-wokwi-pico.log) was blocked on a missing WOKWI_CLI_TOKEN;
#           the maintainer has since created one (personal account, free plan). The token is read
#           inline into wokwi-cli's environment only and appears nowhere in this log.
# wokwi-cli: 0.29.1 (0aa185144b92), wokwi-cli-linuxstatic-x64,
#           sha256 3c9d6da007d008a3822ab468318037285440055132c59fd659d7306e40f14258 (same binary as the first run)
#           server: "Wokwi Simulation API 1.0.0-20261026-g45f2303e"
# zephyr:   3.7.0, SDK 0.16.8, hal_rpi_pico fba7162cc7bee06d0149622bbcaac4e41062d368 (ZEPHYR_EXTRA_MODULES)
# rust:     nightly-2026-04-11 + thumbv6m-none-eabi
# app:      examples/zephyr/c/talker, CONF_FILE="prj.conf;prj-zenoh.conf;<spike>/rpi_pico/serial.conf"
#           (CONFIG_NROS_TRANSPORT_SERIAL=y, CONFIG_NETWORKING=n, CONFIG_UART_INTERRUPT_DRIVEN=y,
#           CONFIG_MAIN_THREAD_PRIORITY=5, CONFIG_HEAP_MEM_POOL_SIZE=16384 -- the Nucleo spike's shape)
# diagram:  one part, "board-pi-pico-w"; pico:GP0 -> $serialMonitor:RX, pico:GP1 -> $serialMonitor:TX, 115200
#
# commands (spike scripts under tmp/spike-524/scripts, not committed):
#   west build -b rpi_pico/rp2040/w examples/zephyr/c/talker -- \
#       -DCONF_FILE=... -DCONFIG_NROS_ZENOH_LOCATOR='"serial/uart@40034000#baudrate=115200"' \
#       -DZEPHYR_EXTRA_MODULES="<repo>;<ws>/modules/hal/rpi_pico;<spike>/atomic-shim" \
#       -DDTC_OVERLAY_FILE=<spike>/rpi_pico/app-u0.overlay \
#       -DNROS_OVERRIDE_ZENOH_MAX_LARGE_SUBSCRIBERS=0 -DNROS_OVERRIDE_ZENOH_MAX_SUBSCRIBERS=1 \
#       -DNROS_OVERRIDE_ZENOH_SERVICE_BUFFER_SIZE=1024 -DNROS_OVERRIDE_ZEPHYR_HEAP_SIZE=32768 \
#       -DNROS_OVERRIDE_ZENOH_MAX_QUERYABLES=1 -DCONFIG_TICKLESS_KERNEL=n
#   socat PTY,link=<run>/zlink,rawer,echo=0 'OPEN:<run>/out.fifo,rdwr!!OPEN:<run>/in.fifo,rdwr'
#   rmw_zenohd (resolved by nros_zenohd_bin; i.e. `ros2 run rmw_zenoh_cpp rmw_zenohd`) with
#       listen/endpoints=["serial/<run>/zlink#baudrate=115200","tcp/127.0.0.1:17491"], multicast scouting off
#   ros2 topic echo /chatter std_msgs/msg/String   (rmw_zenoh_cpp, connect tcp/127.0.0.1:17491 only)
#   WOKWI_CLI_TOKEN=<inline> wokwi-cli -q --interactive --timeout 120000 <proj> <>in.fifo 1<>out.fifo
#
# The link: Wokwi's serial monitor is UART0 (GP0/GP1). `--interactive` puts wokwi-cli's stdin on the
# UART's RX and the serial monitor on its stdout, both byte-transparent (0x00 survives: see step 4),
# so socat turns the pair into a host pty and the router opens it as a serial locator -- the same
# shape as the Nucleo chapter, with wokwi-cli in place of the ST-LINK VCP. The console moves to UART1
# (GP4/GP5), which Wokwi does not show; on the bench UART0 is the GP0/GP1 header pins, so the zenoh
# link needs a USB-to-UART adapter there (the Pico W's USB port is not that UART).

=== 1. build: what the ELF needed (in order of discovery) ===
a. nros_detect_rust_target() has no Cortex-M0+ arm (the first run's finding): the Rust lane fell
   through to the host triple and cc-rs handed arm-zephyr-eabi-gcc `-m64`.
   SPIKE PATCH (reverted, not committed):
       elseif(CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M0PLUS OR CONFIG_CPU_CORTEX_M0)
           set(NROS_RUST_TARGET "thumbv6m-none-eabi" PARENT_SCOPE)
b. thumbv6m has no CAS (`target_has_atomic = "ptr"` is false), and two sites use core atomics RMW:
       error[E0425]: cannot find function `install_log_crate_bridge` in module `nros_log::log_compat`
          --> packages/platform/nros-platform-cffi/src/log.rs:122:35   (callee is cfg(target_has_atomic = "ptr"))
       error[E0599]: no method named `fetch_add` found for struct `Atomic<T>` in the current scope
          --> packages/api/nros-cpp/src/subscription.rs:73:39
   SPIKE PATCH (reverted): gate the first call on target_has_atomic = "ptr"; the second (a
   diagnostics counter) as load + store. With those two the whole Rust lane compiled for thumbv6m.
c. C side: GCC lowers C11 atomic RMW on ARMv6-M to libcalls nobody provides:
       zenoh-pico/src/collections/atomic.c:24: undefined reference to `__atomic_fetch_add_4'
       zenoh-pico/src/collections/atomic.c:27: undefined reference to `__atomic_fetch_sub_4'
       zenoh-pico/src/collections/atomic.c:42: undefined reference to `__atomic_compare_exchange_4'
       zpico-sys/c/zpico/zpico.c:1011: undefined reference to `__atomic_fetch_add_4'
   SPIKE SHIM (tmp only): a Zephyr module with __atomic_{fetch_add,fetch_sub,exchange,compare_exchange}_4
   under irq_lock (correct on the single-core build; the RP2040's second core is not started by Zephyr 3.7).
d. RAM: 264 KiB. Defaults: ``region `RAM' overflowed by 211736 bytes``. The Nucleo ethernet knobs
   (LARGE_SUBSCRIBERS=0, SUBSCRIBERS=1, SERVICE_BUFFER_SIZE=1024, ZEPHYR_HEAP_SIZE=32768) left
   ``region `RAM' overflowed by 16656 bytes``; ZENOH_MAX_QUERYABLES=1 (the talker serves nothing)
   closed it:
       FLASH:      523112 B    2096896 B     24.95%
         RAM:      254888 B       264 KB     94.29%
   Largest remaining: 83,880 B Node::GlobalStorageHolder<0>::storage (executor backing),
   34,512 B nros_platform zephyr_heap HEAP, 32,768 B nros_thread_stacks, 18,592 B g_sessions.

=== 2. Wokwi boots nothing with a tickless kernel (control: Zephyr's own hello_world) ===
$ wokwi-cli --timeout 10000 --expect-text "Hello World" .      # samples/hello_world, board defaults
Wokwi CLI v0.29.1 (0aa185144b92)
Connected to Wokwi Simulation API 1.0.0-20261026-g45f2303e
Starting simulation...

Timeout: simulation did not finish in 10000ms
=> no byte on the serial monitor, same for our talker. Not the wiring: under `wokwi-cli -g`, gdb read
   UART0 CR=0x301 (enabled, TX, RX), IBRD/FBRD 67/52 (115200 at 125 MHz), GPIO0/1 FUNCSEL=2 (UART),
   and every stop landed in the SysTick ISR (sys_clock_announce / sys_clock_set_timeout, ticks=1341)
   with z_sys_post_kernel = false: the kernel never left PRE_KERNEL. Wokwi's SysTick does not carry
   Zephyr 3.7's tickless cortex_m_systick driver.
$ (same, built with -DCONFIG_TICKLESS_KERNEL=n)
*** Booting Zephyr OS build v3.7.0 ***
Hello World! rpi_pico/rp2040/w

Expected text found: "Hello World"
TEST PASSED.
=> the twin needs CONFIG_TICKLESS_KERNEL=n. The bench runs that image too, so "same ELF on bench and
   twin" holds if the descriptor states it for the board; it is not the board default.

