WiFi road: not tried. Serial passed, and the Pico W WiFi through Wokwi needs the private IoT gateway
for a host-local router, which the free (Community) plan does not include (wokwi.com/pricing: only
the shared public gateway; private gateway from Hobby up).

=== plan limits (docs.wokwi.com/wokwi-ci/getting-started, wokwi.com/pricing, read 2026-11-01) ===
free plan: 50 minutes of simulation time per rolling 30-day window, 5 minutes wall clock per session
(Hobby 200 / Hobby+ 500 / Pro 2,000 minutes; sessions 5 / 10 / 50 minutes).
One twin run here: 6 s to the first sample; a 60 s run with setup is about 1 to 1.5 minutes.
Weekly: about 5 runs a month, 5 to 8 minutes of the 50 -- viable, with headroom for reruns, but the
quota is per USER: CI and anyone developing against the same account share it, and the token is a
personal secret a fork-PR job cannot read (schedule/dispatch only). This spike used about 8 minutes.

SPIKE RESULT: PASS (serial road) -- "data: 'Hello World: 1'" from `ros2 topic echo /chatter`, the Pico W
ELF running in Wokwi's cloud sim, zenoh over UART0 -> wokwi-cli --interactive -> host pty -> rmw_zenohd.
Conditions: CONFIG_TICKLESS_KERNEL=n (Wokwi SysTick), zenoh on UART0 with the console on UART1, five
RAM knobs, and three tree gaps patched locally for the spike (Cortex-M0+ Rust triple, two CAS-only
atomic sites, ARMv6-M __atomic libcalls) -- none of which is on main yet.
